    "title": "UMass Amherst Struggles with Drug Scandal and Apartment Blaze - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Katie Knapp ,\n14 hours ago It has been a difficult few weeks for UMass Amherst with two major incidents stemming from their campus. At the end of October, it was revealed that a cocaine string running out of Hotel UMass had been discovered. Hotel UMass is an on-campus hotel that offers all those studying hospitality at the university to gain real experience in the industry. LaMar D. Cook, the former Director of Hotel UMass and former Deputy Director of Governor Maura Healey’s Springfield office, is the alleged perpetrator behind all drug trafficking that occurred through Hotel UMass. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
